(Title) Tj
T*
(Protocol for testing a peer-facilitated behaviour intervention to enhance HIV prevention) Tj
T*
(advocacy and reduce stigma among Ugandan PLHIV) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Background: Community-level HIV prevention remains inadequate in high-prevalence settings.) Tj
T*
(Empowering people living with HIV \(PLHIV\) to serve as prevention advocates may amplify) Tj
T*
(public health impact beyond individual clinical care. Methods: This randomized controlled) Tj
T*
(trial will enrol 210 PLHIV \(105 intervention, 105 control\) and 599 social network members) Tj
T*
(in Uganda. The intervention arm receives an 8-session peer-facilitated curriculum designed) Tj
T*
(to enhance HIV prevention knowledge, build advocacy self-efficacy, reduce internalized) Tj
T*
(stigma, and facilitate disclosure within social networks. Control participants receive) Tj
T*
(standard care. Assessments occur at baseline, 6, 12, and 18 months. Primary outcomes:) Tj
T*
(internalized stigma \(measured by validated scale\) and self-reported prevention advocacy) Tj
T*
(activities in the 12 months preceding follow-up. Secondary outcomes: disclosure patterns) Tj
T*
(among index participants and HIV testing rates and protective behaviours among exposed) Tj
T*
(network members. Proposed sample size of 210 provides 80% power to detect clinically) Tj
T*
(meaningful between-group differences. Analysis will employ mixed-effect models accounting) Tj
T*
(for social network clustering.) Tj
ET
